Z||000033||FieroKyle||12-25-2001||10:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> As a group, I feel we are all pretty much a mature bunch even though we bicker every now and again, don't you agree?<BR>(</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, there is I guess. Can't say much on bickering with my part in the Mustang flames when they first started, but it looks to be finally over.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> But yeah, your right, most people are not bad at all.<P>Well, in just a couple more hours Christmas is over for another 365 days. Ya made it through. Good to hear that you may see your wife for New Years, should make ya feel better if all goes smooth. Good to hear from ya again Blue. Take care.....<P>Kyle<P>||||reg||7
Z||000034||Indy-2M4||12-26-2001||06:35 AM||||OK, Blue...you had better darned well be there.....you made it through Christmas and this is a new day, see? Just one day at a time. You know what? Your gonna make it into the New Year too. We're here for you.||||reg||1
Z||000035||ChadMan||12-26-2001||10:38 AM||||I had been away from this Forum for a couple of months and forgotten what a great bunch of people Fierophiles really are.<P>blue, I hope things start looking up for you soon, buddy.  Obviously your family loves you -- that's why you haven't done yourself in already, right?  Hope 2002 brings better things for you.||||reg||14
Z||000036||fierobaby||12-26-2001||01:49 PM||||well I asume blue you off in chicago by now but I just wanted to say I'm really glad you are still here and trust me take bills advice! it works... :-)<P>lova ya<P>||||reg||1
Z||000037||84Bill||12-31-2001||09:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by blue000:<BR><B>Thank you guy's you have made a bad time bearable. I'm glad I'm not alone in a time like this. I'm not doing great, but I'm still around.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey I like about 70% of what you wrote here, it would be 100% if you removed the <B>NOT</B> from those statements above.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Even if it is not how you feel, just keep saying "I am OK" and "I will be OK" don't say "I am NOT helpless" or "I am NOT alone" because your mind will only see the negative side. You really need to drive the positive home "I AM alone but I AM OK" "it is hard but I will make it" I HAVE friends  <BR>These things are surprisingly hard to do at first. It's hard to reverse years of conditioning but you can do it. You do seem to be doing much better, Keep it up. Just remember you made it happen, we just watched and applauded your courage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000038||blue000||12-31-2001||10:25 AM||||Hello again friends.<P>     It looks like Paxil is kicking in, and my outlook in life is getting better. It is hard to deal with the extreme down and now things are getting better. My wife is in love with me once again, I'm a lot better than just a week ago. I don't want to fool myself into thinking that everything is perfect, my plans now are to come back to Chicago after a couple weeks in California to take care of some stuff, look for a job in Chicago and start from there, as I don't have anything in California at this point. I don't know where things will go from here, but my wife and I want to make things work for us. I want to make things work for me as well. Well once again, thanks guy's for letting me vent and I'm happy to say that it looks like I made it past new years and I'll be around for a while.||||reg||14
Z||000039||84Bill||12-31-2001||11:28 AM||||Most excellent!<BR>The love of a good partner can do wonders especially if they support your needs. Now go out and get Men are from Mars Women are from Venus READ IT and begin to really enjoy the relationship. Please tell me you will keep working on the things I posted it's very important stuff. Much like getting over an illness it takes time to regain strength, you are still a bit on the weak side but at least YOU ARE standing on your feet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> You ARE making progress and you WILL make it. <BR>Nothing is perfect it's only perfect IF you gave it 100% and know you did your best.<P>Again I commend your venture to Cali and attempt at success there. Maybe you should take a look around and see what's there. You may be surprised to find a job before you go back to Chicago  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Never know what lies just beneath your feet.<BR>Did I ever mention the acres of diamonds story?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Happy New Year to you and your wife.||||reg||14
Z||000040||72vinman||12-31-2001||02:49 PM||||Blue, I am glad to see things are beginning to look up for you. I believe the support from a spouse is one of the key factors in helping you pass through the toughest points. Remember "Don't sweat the small stuff"<BR>Try to maintain balance and happiness with your wife and everything else will seem to fall into place. And don't forget to follow Bill's advice. It seems to be working for me.<BR>Have a healthy and prosperous New Year.||||reg||1
Z||000041||hugh||12-31-2001||04:41 PM||||Blue,Since I never experienced what you are now beating I can't offer advice.But what I see is an enormous amount of genuine love and concern for your well being.You are indeed a lucky man to have so many friends.||||reg||14
Z||000042||West Coast Fiero||12-31-2001||04:56 PM||||Blue, your not not alone man, I was diagnosed with clinical deppression 3 years ago and have been on Prozac ever since. It gets hard at times without the meds if you try and go dry, you can find yourself blowing a gasket for nothing or squirting tears over something stupid.<P> Im not sure if any one has heard of Bipolar 2, this is supposed to be a new diagnosis of sorts and my doctor will be testing me for this in late January. If you ever need someone to talk to man, the wen address and phone number are below........<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WestCoast300.gif"> <BR>Eric Nelson<BR>Technician,<BR>West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
